description:
Files: `vibrantix-client-panel/src/components/audit-assurance-2/common/Audit3AttachEvidenceModal.jsx` lines 163–172

Root Cause: The `handleDrop()` function adds all dropped files to `setFiles()` without checking their extension or MIME type. The HTML `accept` attribute on the `<Input type="file">` restricts the file picker dialog but is ignored for drag-and-drop operations. The backend (`evidence-upload.multer.js`) rejects disallowed types, but the user only discovers the rejection after upload submission.

Claude Fix Prompt:
```
Fix D-37 in Audit3AttachEvidenceModal.jsx.

Define the allowed extensions matching the backend ALLOWED_MIME_TYPES:
  const ALLOWED_EXTS = new Set(['.pdf','.doc','.docx','.xls','.xlsx','.ppt','.pptx','.txt','.csv','.jpg','.jpeg','.png','.gif','.zip']);

In handleDrop(), filter dropped files:
  const valid = droppedFiles.filter(f => {
    const ext = '.' + f.name.split('.').pop().toLowerCase();
    return ALLOWED_EXTS.has(ext);
  });
  const rejected = droppedFiles.length - valid.length;
  if (rejected > 0) toast({ title: `${rejected} file(s) rejected`, description: 'Only PDF, Office, image, and ZIP files are allowed', status: 'warning' });
  setFiles(prev => [...prev, ...valid]);

Apply the same check in handleFileChange() for completeness.
```
